  "question": "How should Batch 12JM's legacy Shanghai University locator be reconciled with the library's current 2025.10 newspaper directory, and does SHU's Digital Doubling Platform expose a public remote target object for the 1951 Wenhui issue?",
  "answer": "The 2025.10 SHU newspaper directory preserves the same Shanghai 《文汇报》 coverage 1951(5-8) but gives current rack A7-1 and row codes B/L under 装订馆/收藏馆. The page legend maps B to 新校区期刊室 and L to 嘉定校区期刊室. Therefore Batch 12JM's legacy 6--10 locator remains a prior-directory fact, while present access planning should use the current A7-1 row and B/L metadata. SHU's Digital Doubling Platform is a mediated on-site service: its public page requires email appointment, staff response, then use at a designated terminal on the fifth floor of the main-campus library. The platform page does not name the 1951 Wenhui target, emit a target object ID, or expose a public remote-view contract. No email, appointment, login or other account action was performed.",
